Vivic Research, in collaboration with the Ontario Nonprofit Network, applied the Care Economy Scorecard framework developped by Oxfam and their partners to evaluate Ontario's care economy. This research highlights the gaps in care that Ontarians are currently experiencing and traces their origins back to public policy, declining investment and oversight, and the privatization of care services. The research process included in-depth reviews of provincial policy, employment legislation, and funding documents, as well as consultations with sector experts. 
